  "title": "India's Export Duty Cuts for Petrol and Aviation Fuel",
  "summary": "The Indian government has reduced the export duty on diesel to ₹20 per litre and on aviation fuel to ₹20 per litre, marking significant cuts from previous levels. These measures aim to boost exports while addressing inflationary pressures.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The export duty on diesel has been reduced to ₹20 per litre from ₹25 earlier.",
      "confidence": 0.95
